      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the **Guarded Write Journal** provides rollback capability for file writes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state into an in-memory write journal \u2014 capturing either the file\u0027s previous content or noting that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order:\n- Restoring previous content for files that existed\n- Deleting newly created files\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics**: This provides transactional semantics without needing a database \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held only in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of one run.\n\n**Query agent note**: The Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write capability at all, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
